# Margdarshak — Real-World Implementation Guide
## *How This System Actually Gets Deployed on Indian Roads*

---

## Why Vehicles Are Orange/Red at Junctions — And Why That's Correct

> **This is the most important thing to explain to a judge.**

When you see orange vehicles clustered near a junction:
- **Orange = stopped at a red signal** — this is NORMAL physics
- When the signal turns green, they accelerate → colour shifts to lime → then cyan
- **Cyan = free-flowing traffic** — this is the goal state Margdarshak optimises for

The AI/Backpressure mode **reduces the time vehicles spend orange** by giving green to the most congested approach. Static mode holds all phases for fixed time even if one road is empty — you'll see more orange in static, less in AI mode.

